  "facts": [
    "Korgfjell Tunnel, stretching 8,530 metres, opened on 16 September 2005 after four years of construction that began in September 2001, dramatically reshaping travel along Norway's E6 highway.",
    "By cutting the old 560‑metre‑high, twisting mountain road, the tunnel shaved 4 kilometres off the route and cut travel time by 10–20 minutes, easing a notorious bottleneck for heavy trucks.",
    "The 450‑million‑kroner project replaced a WWII‑era German road that once replaced a ferry at Elsfjord, turning a once‑troublesome stretch into a smooth, year‑round corridor."
